{"item": {"cls": "Item", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/bostonharborislands/items/20599/", "pk": 20599, "company": {"cls": "Company", "uri": "/api/v1/companies/bostonharborislands/", "pk": 6826, "shortname": "bostonharborislands", "name": "Boston Harbor Islands", "processor_currency": "usd", "display_processor_currency": "US dollars"}, "name": "Boston Harbor Lighthouse Cruise", "is_retail": false, "is_archived": false, "is_private": false, "color": 0, "unicode": "Boston Harbor Lighthouse Cruise", "is_bookable_ever_by_phone": true, "sold_out_text": "Trip", "cutoff_unreached_kind": "before-start", "cutoff_unreached_hours": 1.0, "is_cutoff_unreached_call_to_book": true, "cutoff_unreached_call_to_book_text": "", "cutoff_reached_kind": "before-start", "cutoff_reached_hours": 1.0, "is_cutoff_reached_call_to_book": true, "cutoff_reached_call_to_book_text": "", "minimum_initial_party_size": 1, "minimum_subsequent_party_size": 1, "maximum_initial_party_size": null, "maximum_subsequent_party_size": null, "auto_open_kind": "before-start", "auto_open_hours": null, "is_waitlist_when_full": false, "is_unlisted": false, "booking_restriction": null, "is_card_required": false, "is_grouped_calendar": false, "is_free_allowed": true, "is_no_tax": true, "sortable_index": 100, "description": "##Rates\n$41 Adults(12 years and older)\n$36 students/military(Must present ID at check-in)\n$36 Seniors(For ages 65 and older)\n$30 kids(4 - 11 years old)\n$0 toddlers (3 and under)\n\n##Duration \n2 Hours\n\n\n##About\nTour Highlights:\n\nThis special narrated cruise voyages through maritime history and passes renowned Boston Harbor landmarks  and three-lighthouses of Boston Harbor. This 2-hour cruise will sail past Long Island Light, Graves Light, and Boston Light, America's oldest light station. Narrations and programs on-board provided by staff and volunteers from the National Park Service and United States Coast Guard. ​\n\nPlease Note\n - There is no public access to Little Brewster or Boston Light.\n - Adverse weather conditions can force cancellations. Please check your email and voicemail before your trip. ​\n - There is no food or water available on the boat. Feel free to bring your own snacks and meals. \n - Alcohol, smoking and vaping are prohibited on the boat.\n- Tours on August 19 at 3:15 will be held in Spanish", "description_text": "", "description_bullets": "", "seo_description": "", "location": "", "booking_notes": "#Check-In Information\n>All tours depart from the Boston Harbor Island Welcome Center on the Rose Kennedy Greenway at 191w Atlantic Avenue, Boston, MA 02110, directly across from the Long Wharf Marriott, Quincy Market and Aquarium MBTA Stop. Please arrive at least 30 minutes prior to your departure time, tours WILL NOT wait for tardy individuals. If you arrive less than 15 minutes before your tour, you will not be able to board.\n> The Boston Waterfront, is convenient to public transportation. The Aquarium Station lets out across the street from the Welcome Center.  South Station (on the Red Line and Commuter Rail) is a short walk (20 min). There are several parking lots nearby and are within a 5-10 minute walk; fees vary. \n\nBoston traffic can be very congested, please plan accordingly.\n[![Description of image](https://d1a2dkr8rai8e2.cloudfront.net/api/file/k96lL2jiRBaBSsuzGT0Q)](https://goo.gl/maps/mrdZmD1T7LL2)", "cancellation_notes": "#Cancellation policy\nBoston Light tickets are non-refundable 12 hours after purchase. If in the case of unsafe seas or reasons determined by the US Coast Guard or captain, visitor will be fully refunded or given the option to reschedule.\n\nTrips run rain or shine, please plan accordingly.", "no_transportation_notes": "", "no_transportation_minutes": 30, "headline": "Boston's only lighthouse tour with the United States Coast Guard and National Park Service |All Ages", "short_description": null, "image_url": "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/uPWQObqgTmqz0dpROk1x", "image_cdn_url": "https://cdn.fil